  """
// Theorem 12.8 (Canopy Symmetry).
// The canopy of any structure S is symmetric about its structural
// center. Every asymmetry in a subsystem is balanced by complementary
// asymmetry elsewhere in the canopy.
//
// Net asymmetry would be structure from nothing (violating Law 2).
// The complete canopy, summed over all traces, reproduces exactly the
// structural content of S with no remainder and no deficit.
//
// Corollary 12.9 (Asymmetry Implies Complement): if a shape system
// exhibits asymmetry X, the canopy contains complementary -X.
//
// Theorem 12.11 (Asymmetry-Canopy Equivalence): for a constructed
// projection, the asymmetry profile fully determines the canopy.
//
// Derives from: theory.branching.canopy, theory.coherence.law2
  """
